;; The module math (PY5e, part 2b; Modules/mathmodule.c): the functions CPython takes from the C library
;; are Go's math for now, their last digit classed, until the shared musl libm (go/arbace/libm, the user's
;; decision on PY5b's DECISION 1 (a)) is bit-exact on arm64 too (mac/189-libm-fma); the exact ones (sqrt, floor, fmod, frexp ...) and the integer ones are Go's and CPython's
;; own algorithms. log2, log10, exp2, cbrt, erf, erfc, gamma and lgamma wait for their musl ports (or
;; CPython's own gamma code): they raise NotImplementedError naming the port.

